 }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot {{field-2}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315077 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d7d424ca-a5eb-5340-a732-023666fa3414" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315077 #edb/ref 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe use the integration by parts: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x+1\\, & ⇒\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(uv\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{n}[(3x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }-\\frac{3}{n}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(((3\\pi +1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{3}{n}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)]_{0}^{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{n\\pi }(0+\\frac{3}{n}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )-1)}{{n}^{2}\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi )=(-1)^{n},$ we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{6((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the Fourier cosine series is\n\n$$\nf(x)∼(1+\\frac{3}{2}\\pi )+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6((-1)^{n}-1)}{\\pi {n}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86b3942b-d5fe-58b1-8280-9f2a9124377a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186315080 #edb/ref 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(4\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\sqrt{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186514489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186514492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186514524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186514538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186514545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1045 "Fourier Cosine Series" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186514545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186513518 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8229b7db-f15f-558a-b67e-bb5853ab5391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186